course: dictionary
lesson: 6505
title: The old word needful
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Needful is an old-fashioned word that means needed or necessary. You will mostly find it in old books and in the Bible. «One thing is needful» means one thing is necessary, one thing must be done. The words around it give you the clue.
explain: Today most people say needed or necessary instead. Try swapping the word into the sentence: «One thing is necessary» still makes sense, so needful means necessary here. This is the swap check from the last lesson.
explain: In informal British English, the needful is a noun meaning what is needed, often money. «Dad will provide the needful» means Dad will provide what is needed. Check the sentence to see whether the word is describing something or naming a thing.
explain: In Indian English, «Please do the needful» is a polite, common phrase in emails. It means please do what is necessary. Many English speakers elsewhere find it old-fashioned, so it may sound strange to you.
fact: Needful means needed or necessary.
fact: «One thing is needful» means one thing is necessary.
fact: The needful is an informal UK noun meaning what is needed, often money.
fact: «Do the needful» is common in Indian English and means do what is necessary.
fact: Needful is old-fashioned, so today people usually say needed or necessary.
exercise: «One thing is needful.» What does needful mean here? | Foolish | *Necessary | Hungry | Far away
exercise: «Dad will provide the needful.» In this sentence, what is the needful most likely to be? | *Something needed, often money | A song | A joke | A boat
exercise: Priya's email says «Please do the needful.» What does she mean? | Please buy a new computer | Please go to bed early | Please forget the email | *Please do what is necessary
test: Which everyday word could replace needful in «Warm clothes are needful in winter»? | Sleepy | Coloured | *Necessary | Silly
test: Why might a modern writer say necessary instead of needful? | Because needful means happy | *Because needful is old-fashioned and rare in everyday talk | Because needful is a country | Because necessary is a noun
exam: Which is the best meaning of «needful» in «Is there anything else needful before we leave?» | *Necessary | Pleasant | Loud | Dangerous
